From 4acf8ce9d7951ddba3039733dad3c63ff1ae8c54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kamalbuilds <geniusamansingh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:30:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(examples): merkle_pull_claim, a Merkle root registry and
 a pull-claim pool

RootRegistry takes a payout root from two of three operator keys, holds it through an audit window
the chain enforces with this.age, and activates it for anyone once the window has passed; a guardian
key can cancel a pending root. FoldClaimPool pays each leaf of the active root once, as the
difference to what the leaf already claimed, to its own locking bytecode (method 0) or to the
destination its legacy key signs for (method 1), and keeps the receipt in a mapping.

The test lives in examples/testing-suite: it compiles both contracts and runs the window, a
cancel, a stranger relaying a claim, forged claims and a cumulative top-up on the mock network.
Activating a root uses setSequence, so this builds on the stateful setSequence call option.
