 </div>
 
 Unspent Phi allows users to convert Bitcoin Cash they have today into a series of periodic payments over a long period of time.  It's a set of simple contracts that rely on rolling timelocks and introspection rather than signatures; meaning as long as the correct recipients are paid, anyone may build and submit transactions.
+
+## Merkle pull claims
+
+A registry publishes a payout Merkle root after a public audit window that the chain itself enforces, and a pool pays any leaf of the active root once, to the identity the leaf names. Recipients, or anyone relaying for them, pull their own reward in one transaction, so the operator never sends a transaction per recipient. A leaf can be keyed to a locking bytecode or to the hash160 of a legacy public key whose holder signs the claim and picks the destination. The two contracts and their test suite are in [`examples/merkle_pull_claim`](https://github.com/solidcash/solidcash/tree/master/examples/merkle_pull_claim).
